B.HF=new A.ha(B.bu,B.ay,"Mercury conjunct Moon blends thinking and feeling closely \u2014 emotions get put into words easily and quickly, though sometimes before they've been fully processed.",!1)
B.HJ=new A.ha(B.aj,B.aQ,"Sun conjunct Venus (astronomically, these two are never far apart) fuses identity closely with charm, aesthetics, and the desire to be liked \u2014 warmth becomes a core part of how someone presents themselves.",!1)
B.HB=new A.ha(B.aV,B.ch,"Mars conjunct Pluto fuses ordinary drive with real intensity \u2014 a formidable combination of willpower, though one that benefits from a conscious outlet rather than being left to simmer.",!1)
B.a_y=s([B.HF,B.HJ,B.HB],t.On)
B.HP=new A.q7(B.eX,"A conjunction happens when two points sit at (or very near) the same ecliptic degree \u2014 the closest and most concentrated aspect, blending both planets' energies into a single, hard-to-separate combined force. It is not inherently harmonious or difficult; the blend is simply intense, and its quality depends heavily on which two planets are involved.","A natal conjunction fuses two planetary themes into one persistent personality trait \u2014 the two planets tend to act together automatically, for better or worse, rather than as separable influences a person can easily distinguish in themselves.","A transiting conjunction to a natal point marks a short window where that placement is directly activated and intensified \u2014 often the start of a new cycle involving whatever that natal point represents.",'Because a conjunction blends rather than balances, the most useful question is usually "which of these two energies is currently running the show, and does the other one need more conscious room?"',B.a_y)
B.HG=new A.ha(B.aQ,B.aV,"Venus sextile Mars supports easy, healthy chemistry between affection and drive \u2014 attraction and pursuit work well together without much friction.",!1)
B.HH=new A.ha(B.bu,B.bR,"Mercury sextile Jupiter supports optimistic, big-picture thinking that's still reasonably grounded \u2014 a good combination for teaching, writing, or planning.",!1)
B.a6w=s([B.HG,B.HH],t.On)
B.HQ=new A.q7(B.eY,"A sextile is a 60\xb0 angle, traditionally read as a harmonious, gently supportive aspect \u2014 easier and more available than a trine, but requiring a bit more active choice to use well rather than arriving as effortlessly.","A natal sextile shows a talent or supportive resource between two planets that works well once engaged \u2014 it rarely causes problems on its own, but also rarely insists on being used the way a square or conjunction might.","A transiting sextile to a natal point offers a supportive, low-friction window to make progress on that placement's themes \u2014 a good moment to take a small deliberate step rather than wait for the opportunity to knock harder.","Because sextiles are gentle rather than insistent, they reward active follow-through \u2014 noticing the opportunity and actually taking it, rather than assuming it will happen on its own.",B.a6w)
B.HL=new A.ha(B.aV,B.b4,"Mars square Saturn pits drive against restriction \u2014 frustrating when action feels blocked, but capable of producing real discipline and staying power once the friction is channeled rather than fought.",!1)
B.HA=new A.ha(B.aj,B.ay,"Sun square Moon (common near a chart's first-quarter-Moon-like configurations) shows tension between conscious identity and instinctive emotional needs \u2014 integrating both, rather than favoring one, is the long-term work.",!1)
B.HM=new A.ha(B.aQ,B.ch,"Venus square Pluto brings intensity and possessiveness into love and value \u2014 capable of deep, transformative bonds, but prone to power struggles if trust isn't consciously built.",!1)
B.QB=s([B.HL,B.HA,B.HM],t.On)
B.HS=new A.q7(B.eZ,"A square is a 90\xb0 angle, traditionally read as a challenging, friction-generating aspect \u2014 the two planets involved want genuinely different things, and that tension has to be actively worked with rather than ignored.","A natal square shows an internal tension between two placements that tends to recur throughout life until it's consciously addressed \u2014 often a source of real personal growth precisely because it can't simply be avoided.","A transiting square to a natal point marks a pressured window where that placement's themes are actively tested \u2014 uncomfortable in the moment, but often when real, lasting change actually gets made.","Squares respond best to direct, conscious engagement \u2014 naming the tension explicitly and choosing a constructive outlet for it tends to work far better than hoping the friction quietly resolves itself.",B.QB)
B.HN=new A.ha(B.aQ,B.bR,"Venus trine Jupiter brings natural warmth, generosity, and good fortune in love and finances \u2014 genuinely one of the more universally pleasant aspects to have.",!1)
B.HI=new A.ha(B.ay,B.cr,"Moon trine Neptune brings easy emotional sensitivity, compassion, and imagination \u2014 a natural gift for empathy and creative or spiritual insight.",!1)
B.HK=new A.ha(B.aj,B.b4,"Sun trine Saturn brings natural discipline and reliability to core identity \u2014 steady follow-through that others tend to trust without needing to be convinced of it.",!1)
B.X8=s([B.HN,B.HI,B.HK],t.On)
B.HO=new A.q7(B.f_,"A trine is a 120\xb0 angle, traditionally read as the most effortlessly harmonious aspect \u2014 the two planets involved naturally support and understand each other, often to the point that the talent involved is used without much conscious effort at all.","A natal trine shows an area of natural ease or talent between two placements \u2014 genuinely valuable, though sometimes so effortless it goes underdeveloped simply because it never demanded attention the way a harder aspect would.","A transiting trine to a natal point offers a smooth, supportive window for that placement's themes \u2014 good timing, low friction, and worth actively using rather than merely enjoying passively.","Because trines come easily, the main risk is complacency \u2014 deliberately investing effort in a trine's natural talent usually pays off far more than letting it coast.",B.X8)
B.HC=new A.ha(B.b4,B.aj,'A transiting Saturn opposite natal Sun is one of astrology\'s classic "reality check" transits \u2014 a pressured but valuable window for testing whether current commitments and self-image actually hold up under real responsibility.',!0)
B.HE=new A.ha(B.aQ,B.aV,"Venus opposite Mars highlights the push and pull between wanting harmony and wanting to assert desire directly \u2014 common in dynamic, magnetic partnerships that still need active balancing to avoid a push-pull pattern.",!1)
B.HD=new A.ha(B.ay,B.b4,"Moon opposite Saturn shows tension between emotional needs and self-discipline or duty \u2014 often felt as loneliness until both sides (feeling and structure) are given real, conscious room.",!1)
B.Tu=s([B.HC,B.HE,B.HD],t.On)
B.HR=new A.q7(B.f0,"An opposition is a 180\xb0 angle, traditionally read as a challenging aspect of balance and awareness \u2014 the two planets pull toward opposite poles, and the real work is integrating both rather than collapsing into just one side.","A natal opposition often shows up first as a tension projected onto other people or outer circumstances (relationships are a common stage for it) before it's recognized as an internal polarity that needs balancing within the individual themselves.","A transiting opposition to a natal point marks a window where that placement's themes are directly confronted, often through an external situation or person that forces a choice or a genuine reckoning.","Oppositions respond best to deliberately honoring both ends rather than picking a side \u2014 the goal is a working balance, not a winner.",B.Tu)
