B.aiI=new A.by([B.eM,B.XR,B.eN,B.a_n,B.eO,B.QW,B.eP,B.TI,B.eQ,B.Wu,B.eR,B.UH,B.eS,B.a2l,B.dT,B.a2G,B.eT,B.YZ,B.eU,B.RY,B.dR,B.WF,B.dS,B.Qv],A.a6("by<dB,J<M>>"))
B.aye=new A.iy(B.eM,"Aries opens the zodiac wheel as its first sign, and carries the unmistakable energy of a beginning. Ruled by Mars and driven by raw, cardinal fire, Aries acts first and reflects afterward, treating every new day as an invitation to start something.","Courageous, direct, and instinctively decisive, Aries moves toward challenges that make others hesitate. This sign brings initiative, physical vitality, and an honest, uncomplicated enthusiasm that can energize an entire room or project.","Impatience is Aries' most familiar obstacle \u2014 waiting for the right moment rarely feels as satisfying as acting immediately. This can tip into impulsiveness, a short temper, or abandoning things once the initial thrill of newness fades.","Aries feels quickly and expresses just as quickly; there is little gap between emotion and reaction. Anger passes almost as fast as it arrives, and Aries rarely holds a grudge, preferring to resolve tension head-on rather than let it simmer.","Blunt, energetic, and to the point, Aries says what it means without much preamble. This directness reads as refreshing honesty to some and as abruptness to others, especially in situations that call for diplomacy over speed.","Aries falls fast and pursues openly, thriving on the chase and the thrill of a new connection. A partner who can match its pace and directness \u2014 while offering their own independence \u2014 keeps the spark alive long after the initial rush.","As a friend, Aries is loyal, protective, and always ready to show up for the people it cares about, often literally \u2014 showing up in person, ready to help. Friendships stay lively when there is room for spontaneity and shared activity, not just quiet company.","Within family life, Aries often takes on a protective, sometimes assertive role, pushing relatives toward action and change. Patience with slower family rhythms can be a genuine practice area, especially when a household values consensus over quick decisions.","Aries excels where initiative is rewarded: launching new ventures, leading teams into uncharted territory, or working independently toward a visible goal. Roles with clear competition, physical engagement, or the freedom to act on instinct suit this sign well.","Financially, Aries tends toward impulsive spending on whatever feels exciting in the moment, and can be quick to take financial risks in pursuit of a big win. Building even a small habit of pausing before a purchase goes a long way toward steadier finances.","Creative expression for Aries is bold, physical, and often improvisational \u2014 first drafts and first takes carry real energy. This sign thrives when creativity does not require excessive planning before the first mark is made.","Aries approaches spirituality actively rather than contemplatively, often finding meaning through movement, ritual action, or direct personal experience rather than long stillness. Fire-ritual and movement-based practices tend to resonate more than passive study.","Aries generally sparks easily with fellow fire signs Leo and Sagittarius, who match its pace and enthusiasm. Air signs Gemini and Aquarius can keep up mentally and add useful perspective, while earth and water signs offer grounding that Aries benefits from, even when it initially resists the slower tempo.","Unchecked, Aries' shadow shows up as self-centered impulsiveness, a need to always be first or right, and a willingness to steamroll others' pace or opinions in pursuit of its own momentum.","Aries grows by learning that not every situation needs an immediate reaction, and that patience is not the same as weakness. Real mastery comes from channeling its fire deliberately rather than simply reacting to whatever appears first.")
B.ayd=new A.iy(B.eN,"Taurus follows Aries with a steadying, fixed-earth presence, ruled by Venus and grounded in the physical, sensory world. Where Aries starts, Taurus builds \u2014 slowly, deliberately, and with lasting materials.","Reliable, patient, and remarkably persistent, Taurus finishes what it starts and rarely abandons a commitment. This sign brings a grounding steadiness to any group, along with genuine appreciation for comfort, beauty, and quality.","Taurus' fixed nature can calcify into stubbornness, a resistance to change that outlasts its usefulness, or a reluctance to leave comfortable-but-unfulfilling situations simply because they are familiar.","Emotionally steady and slow to be provoked, Taurus prefers a calm, predictable inner life. Once genuinely upset, however, this sign can hold onto the feeling for a long time, needing real reassurance before it fully settles.","Taurus communicates in a measured, practical way, preferring concrete facts over abstract theorizing. It can take real time to form an opinion, but once formed, that opinion is stated plainly and defended firmly.","In love, Taurus is sensual, devoted, and looking for something built to last rather than a fleeting spark. Physical affection, shared meals, and consistent presence matter more to this sign than grand romantic gestures.","Taurus friendships form slowly and run deep; this sign is not interested in a wide social circle so much as a small number of people it can trust completely. Dependability is the currency of Taurus friendship, offered and expected in equal measure.","At home, Taurus values tradition, routine, and physical comfort, often becoming the family member who maintains rituals and keeps the household running smoothly. Stability at home directly supports this sign's sense of wellbeing everywhere else.","Taurus thrives in roles that reward consistency and craftsmanship: finance, agriculture, design, culinary work, or any field where patient, hands-on effort compounds into visible, tangible results over time.","Financially, Taurus is typically the most naturally cautious sign, preferring savings and tangible assets over speculative risk. This sign's challenge is loosening its grip enough to enjoy resources, not merely accumulate them.","Creative work for Taurus is tactile and sensory \u2014 working with textiles, food, music, or physical materials that can be touched, shaped, and refined slowly until they feel genuinely finished.","Taurus finds the sacred in the physical world itself: a garden, a meal prepared with care, a walk outdoors. Grounding, body-based practices tend to resonate far more than abstract or purely intellectual spiritual frameworks.","Taurus pairs comfortably with fellow earth signs Virgo and Capricorn, who share its practical values. Water signs Cancer and Pisces offer emotional depth that Taurus finds nourishing, while Libra, its fellow Venus-ruled sign, shares its appreciation for beauty and harmony.","Taurus' shadow side surfaces as possessiveness, rigid stubbornness, or a materialism that mistakes accumulation for security, resisting any change even when change is clearly overdue.","Growth for Taurus means learning that security can coexist with change, and that letting go of what no longer serves it is not a loss but a form of tending the garden.")
B.ayj=new A.iy(B.eO,"Gemini is the zodiac's great communicator: a mutable air sign ruled by Mercury, endlessly curious, and most alive in the exchange of ideas. Where Taurus settles, Gemini circulates.","Quick-witted, adaptable, and genuinely curious about nearly everything, Gemini brings versatility and mental agility to any situation. This sign connects people and ideas that would otherwise never meet.","Gemini's restlessness can read as inconsistency \u2014 enthusiasm that fades once the novelty wears off, or a tendency to know a little about everything without going deep into anything in particular.","Gemini processes feelings through thought and conversation rather than sitting with them silently. Talking something through, often from multiple angles, is how this sign metabolizes an emotional experience.","Communication is Gemini's natural domain: witty, fast-moving, and genuinely enjoyable, with a gift for adapting tone and content to whoever it is speaking with. This sign can talk its way into or out of nearly anything.","In love, Gemini needs mental stimulation as much as romantic connection \u2014 a partner who can hold an interesting conversation matters enormously. Variety and playfulness keep a Gemini relationship feeling alive.","Gemini tends to maintain a wide, varied circle of friends across many different social worlds, genuinely enjoying the contrast between them. This sign is the connector who introduces people who would never otherwise meet.","At home, Gemini often plays the role of the family's news source and mediator, translating between generations or viewpoints. Restlessness with rigid family routines is common, alongside a real love of lively, talkative gatherings.","Gemini flourishes in writing, media, teaching, sales, or any field built on communication and variety. Roles that involve repetitive, solitary tasks with little intellectual stimulation tend to drain this sign quickly.","Financially, Gemini can be inconsistent \u2014 sharp with a good deal one moment, impulsive the next \u2014 and benefits from simple, low-effort systems that keep spending on track without requiring constant attention.","Creativity flows through language and idea-connection for Gemini: writing, comedy, podcasting, or any medium that rewards quick thinking and the ability to hold several ideas in play at once.","Gemini approaches spirituality intellectually at first, drawn to studying many traditions rather than committing early to one. Meaning tends to arrive through understanding and discussion rather than silent devotion.","Gemini connects naturally with fellow air signs Libra and Aquarius, who share its love of ideas. Fire signs Aries and Leo match its energy and spontaneity, while a grounded earth or water sign partner can help Gemini follow through on what it starts.","Gemini's shadow includes superficiality, two-facedness, or using wit and charm to avoid emotional depth and genuine commitment altogether.","Gemini grows by choosing depth in at least a few areas of life, proving to itself that sustained focus does not have to mean losing its love of variety.")
B.ayc=new A.iy(B.eP,"Cancer is the zodiac's emotional anchor: a cardinal water sign ruled by the Moon, oriented around home, family, and the deep undercurrents of feeling that most signs keep hidden.","Deeply nurturing, intuitive, and fiercely loyal, Cancer creates genuine emotional safety for the people it loves. This sign remembers what matters to others and shows care through consistent, attentive action.","Cancer's sensitivity can tip into moodiness, defensiveness, or retreating into its shell at the first sign of perceived rejection, sometimes reading threat into situations that were never meant that way.","Cancer feels everything intensely and holds onto emotional memories longer than most signs, for better and worse. Its moods can shift like tides, often in response to the emotional atmosphere around it rather than to logic.","Cancer communicates through tone and feeling as much as words, picking up on unspoken emotional undercurrents in a conversation. Directness about its own needs can be difficult; hints and gestures often come first.","In love, Cancer is devoted, protective, and looking for a true emotional home with another person. It needs consistent reassurance and gentle care, especially early on, before it fully opens up.","Cancer friendships feel like family \u2014 this sign remembers birthdays, shows up during hard times, and quietly keeps a group connected. Feeling truly needed and valued matters more to Cancer than the size of its social circle.","Family is often the center of Cancer's entire world, and this sign frequently becomes the one who holds the family together across generations, preserving traditions, recipes, and shared history.","Cancer does well in caregiving, hospitality, counseling, or any field built around nurturing others and creating a sense of belonging. A workplace that feels emotionally cold rarely brings out this sign's best work.","Financially, Cancer is protective and security-minded, often saving toward home and family rather than personal indulgence. Emotional spending \u2014 comfort purchases during difficult moods \u2014 is this sign's most common financial pitfall.","Cancer's creativity is deeply personal and often autobiographical: cooking, photography, music, or writing that processes memory and feeling rather than pursuing pure technical mastery.","Cancer's spiritual life is intuitive and tied closely to ancestry, home, and the cycles of the Moon. Ritual around family, memory, and emotional healing tends to resonate more than intellectual frameworks.","Cancer bonds deeply with fellow water signs Scorpio and Pisces, who understand its emotional depth intuitively. Earth signs Taurus and Virgo offer the stability Cancer craves, while a fire or air sign partner can help this sign come out of its shell more often.","Cancer's shadow includes emotional manipulation, guilt-tripping, or clinging to old hurts as a way of controlling how close others are allowed to get.","Cancer grows by learning that vulnerability shared openly is stronger than protection maintained through withdrawal, and that not every perceived slight requires retreat.")
B.aya=new A.iy(B.eQ,"Leo is the zodiac's radiant heart: a fixed fire sign ruled by the Sun, built for genuine self-expression, generosity, and being fully, unapologetically seen.","Warm, confident, and naturally generous, Leo brings genuine warmth and encouragement to everyone around it. This sign leads with creativity and heart, and is remarkably loyal to the people it considers its own.","Leo's need for recognition can tip into pride, a difficulty accepting criticism, or dominating a room in ways that leave little space for quieter voices to be heard.","Leo feels things vividly and expresses emotion openly and dramatically rather than concealing it. Being ignored or dismissed wounds this sign far more deeply than open conflict ever does.","Leo communicates with warmth, storytelling flair, and genuine enthusiasm, naturally drawing attention when it speaks. Feedback lands best when it is delivered with the same warmth Leo offers others.","In love, Leo is romantic, generous, and loyal, showing affection boldly and expecting genuine admiration in return. A partner who celebrates Leo openly \u2014 and lets Leo celebrate them just as loudly \u2014 keeps this sign deeply devoted.","Leo is the friend who shows up with full-hearted enthusiasm, celebrates others' wins as if they were its own, and expects similar loyalty in return. Being taken for granted is this sign's fastest route to real hurt.","At home, Leo often becomes the family's proud center \u2014 generous with time and resources, and quick to defend family members fiercely against outside criticism, even while pushing them toward their own brightest potential.","Leo thrives in leadership, performance, or any visible role where its creativity and confidence can shine, from management to the arts. Roles that keep this sign anonymous or invisible rarely satisfy it for long.","Financially, Leo enjoys generosity and quality, sometimes spending more than planned on gestures that make others feel special. Building modest financial discipline lets this sign keep giving without strain.","Creativity is central to Leo's identity \u2014 performance, design, or any bold, visible art form where its personal signature is unmistakable and its passion is on full display.","Leo's spirituality often centers on personal purpose and creative self-expression as a sacred act. Practices that let this sign feel like the hero of a meaningful story resonate strongly.","Leo pairs naturally with fellow fire signs Aries and Sagittarius, matching its energy and enthusiasm. Air signs Gemini and Libra appreciate its warmth and wit, while an Aquarius partner \u2014 its opposite sign \u2014 offers a compelling balance of individuality and togetherness.","Leo's shadow shows up as vanity, a need for constant validation, or an inability to share the spotlight even when the moment genuinely calls for it.","Leo grows by learning that its worth does not depend on applause, and that genuine generosity means celebrating others even when no one is celebrating Leo back.")
B.ayg=new A.iy(B.eR,"Virgo is the zodiac's devoted craftsperson: a mutable earth sign ruled by Mercury, oriented toward refinement, service, and getting the details genuinely right.","Analytical, meticulous, and quietly dependable, Virgo notices what others miss and steadily improves whatever it touches. This sign's practical helpfulness is often the invisible reason things run smoothly.","Virgo's eye for detail can curdle into perfectionism, harsh self-criticism, or an anxious need to control small details that ultimately don't matter as much as this sign fears they do.","Virgo tends to process emotion through analysis, sometimes overthinking a feeling rather than simply sitting with it. Genuine care is expressed through useful, practical action more often than open emotional declaration.","Precise, thoughtful, and often quite modest, Virgo chooses words carefully and prefers accuracy over exaggeration. Blunt honesty from Virgo is usually intended as genuine helpfulness, not criticism for its own sake.","In love, Virgo shows devotion through small, consistent acts of service rather than grand declarations. It needs a partner who notices and appreciates those quiet efforts, rather than dismissing them as unremarkable.","Virgo is the friend who remembers the practical details \u2014 the allergy, the deadline, the small preference \u2014 and quietly acts on them. This sign's loyalty shows up as consistent usefulness rather than loud declarations of affection.","At home, Virgo often becomes the organizer and quiet problem-solver, managing logistics that keep the household functioning. Learning to ask for help, rather than simply doing everything itself, is a common family-life lesson.","Virgo excels in fields that reward precision and care: healthcare, editing, research, quality control, or any role where getting the details right genuinely matters to the outcome.","Financially, Virgo is typically careful and well-organized, tracking spending closely and rarely making impulsive purchases. This sign's challenge is loosening its grip enough to spend on genuine enjoyment, not just necessity.","Virgo's creativity shows through craftsmanship and revision \u2014 writing, textile work, or design where patient refinement produces something quietly excellent rather than flashy.","Virgo's spiritual practice tends to be practical and health-oriented: ritual as routine, service as devotion, and everyday acts of care treated as genuinely sacred.","Virgo pairs comfortably with fellow earth signs Taurus and Capricorn, sharing its practical outlook. Water signs Cancer and Scorpio appreciate its quiet devotion, while a Pisces partner \u2014 its opposite sign \u2014 offers a valuable balance between structure and flow.","Virgo's shadow includes harsh criticism of self or others, controlling behavior disguised as helpfulness, or a nagging inability to ever feel that anything is truly good enough.",'Virgo grows by accepting that "good enough" is sometimes the healthiest outcome, and that its own worth is not contingent on flawless execution.')
B.ayf=new A.iy(B.eS,"Libra is the zodiac's diplomat: a cardinal air sign ruled by Venus, oriented toward balance, fairness, and the art of genuine connection with others.","Charming, fair-minded, and socially graceful, Libra brings harmony and thoughtful perspective to conflicts others struggle to resolve. This sign's natural diplomacy helps people feel genuinely heard.","Libra's desire for balance can become indecisiveness, a tendency to avoid necessary conflict, or people-pleasing that quietly buries its own actual preferences.","Libra often weighs feelings the way it weighs decisions \u2014 considering every angle before settling on how it truly feels, which can create an internal sense of imbalance when a fast reaction is actually needed.","Diplomatic and considerate, Libra chooses words that keep the peace and consider the other person's perspective carefully. This sensitivity to others can occasionally come at the cost of stating its own position clearly.","In love, Libra is romantic, attentive, and genuinely happiest in partnership, sometimes defining itself through its relationships more than through solo pursuits. A partner who values equal give and take keeps this balance healthy.","Libra is the friend who smooths over group tension and makes sure everyone feels included, often serving as a social hub. Genuine reciprocity \u2014 not just pleasant company \u2014 is what keeps a Libra friendship feeling balanced.","At home, Libra often plays the family mediator, easing tension between relatives and advocating for fairness. Learning to state its own needs directly, rather than only smoothing things over for others, is a recurring family lesson.","Libra thrives in law, diplomacy, design, or any collaborative field where fairness and aesthetics matter. Highly competitive or consistently confrontational environments tend to drain this sign's energy quickly.","Financially, Libra enjoys quality and beauty, and can overspend on aesthetics or on generous gestures toward others. A simple, consistent budget helps balance this sign's appreciation for the finer things.","Libra's creativity is aesthetic and relational \u2014 design, styling, or any art form built around balance, proportion, and genuine visual harmony.","Libra's spirituality often centers on justice, harmony, and right relationship \u2014 both with others and within itself \u2014 treating balance as a spiritual practice in its own right.","Libra connects easily with fellow air signs Gemini and Aquarius, sharing its love of ideas and connection. Fire signs Leo and Sagittarius match its warmth, while an Aries partner \u2014 its opposite sign \u2014 offers a compelling balance of independence and partnership.","Libra's shadow includes superficial conflict-avoidance, a hidden resentment that builds when its own needs go unspoken for too long, or vanity that prioritizes appearance over substance.","Libra grows by learning that real harmony sometimes requires necessary conflict first, and that its own preferences deserve equal weight in the balance it works so hard to maintain.")
B.ayh=new A.iy(B.dT,"Scorpio is the zodiac's depth-seeker: a fixed water sign ruled traditionally by Mars and, in modern astrology, by Pluto, drawn toward intensity, transformation, and whatever lies beneath the surface.","Passionate, resilient, and fiercely perceptive, Scorpio sees through pretense and commits completely once it decides something matters. This sign's emotional courage helps it face what others avoid.","Scorpio's intensity can turn into jealousy, secretiveness, or a need for control that emerges from a deep fear of being betrayed or left exposed.","Scorpio feels everything at full depth and rarely does anything halfway, including trust. Once trust is broken, this sign finds it genuinely difficult to fully extend it again.","Scorpio communicates selectively, often revealing only what it chooses to, when it chooses to. Beneath a guarded exterior, this sign is capable of remarkably direct, penetrating honesty once trust is established.","In love, Scorpio bonds intensely and expects total honesty and loyalty in return. Superficial connection holds little appeal \u2014 this sign is looking for a transformative, all-in partnership.","Scorpio friendships form slowly but run extremely deep once trust is earned, and this sign will defend a true friend fiercely. Betrayal, once discovered, is rarely forgotten.","At home, Scorpio often holds the family's deeper emotional truths, sometimes as the one who says what others avoid saying. Learning to soften control in family dynamics is a common lifelong practice.","Scorpio excels in psychology, research, investigation, medicine, or any field that rewards going beneath the surface to uncover what is really happening.","Financially, Scorpio is strategic and can be secretive about resources, often preferring financial independence and private control over shared or transparent arrangements.","Scorpio's creativity channels intensity into transformative work \u2014 writing, music, or visual art that confronts difficult truths rather than staying safely on the surface.","Scorpio's spiritual path is often about death and rebirth in a symbolic sense \u2014 shedding old identities and confronting shadow material directly rather than avoiding it.","Scorpio bonds deeply with fellow water signs Cancer and Pisces, who meet its emotional intensity. Earth signs Taurus and Virgo offer grounding, while a Taurus partner \u2014 its opposite sign \u2014 provides a compelling mix of steadiness and depth.","Scorpio's shadow includes manipulation, obsessive control, or using secrecy as a weapon rather than a form of genuine privacy.","Scorpio grows by learning that vulnerability, offered voluntarily, is more powerful than control maintained through secrecy.")
B.ayb=new A.iy(B.eT,"Sagittarius is the zodiac's philosopher-adventurer: a mutable fire sign ruled by Jupiter, forever chasing the next horizon, the next idea, the next expansion of what feels possible.","Optimistic, adventurous, and refreshingly honest, Sagittarius brings a sense of possibility wherever it goes. This sign's enthusiasm for learning and exploring is genuinely contagious.","Sagittarius' love of freedom can slide into restlessness, a tendency to overcommit and then disappear, or bluntness that lands as tactless when a gentler touch was actually needed.","Sagittarius prefers to keep emotional weather light and moving, often processing difficult feelings through motion, humor, or a change of scenery rather than sitting still with them.","Sagittarius speaks with enthusiasm, humor, and total honesty, sometimes without pausing to consider how blunt that honesty might land on someone more sensitive.","In love, Sagittarius needs a genuine sense of freedom and shared adventure; feeling confined kills the spark fast. A partner who brings their own independent interests keeps this relationship exciting for the long haul.","Sagittarius is the friend who shows up with a new idea, a new trip, or a new perspective, and friendships flourish when there is room for spontaneity and honest, unfiltered conversation.","At home, Sagittarius often pushes the family toward new experiences and broader perspectives, sometimes chafing against overly rigid family traditions or expectations.","Sagittarius thrives in travel, education, publishing, or any field that rewards big-picture thinking and constant learning. Repetitive, tightly confined roles tend to feel stifling fast.","Financially, Sagittarius can be generous and optimistic to a fault, sometimes underestimating costs while chasing the next adventure. A simple travel or experience fund helps this sign plan for what it loves most.","Sagittarius' creativity is expansive and philosophical \u2014 travel writing, storytelling, or any art form that explores big questions and distant places.","Sagittarius approaches spirituality as an ongoing quest, drawn to comparing philosophies and traditions from around the world rather than settling into just one early on.","Sagittarius pairs naturally with fellow fire signs Aries and Leo, sharing its enthusiasm. Air signs Gemini and Aquarius match its love of ideas, while a Gemini partner \u2014 its opposite sign \u2014 offers a stimulating balance of curiosity and expansiveness.","Sagittarius' shadow includes reckless overpromising, tactless honesty used carelessly, or fleeing responsibility the moment it starts to feel confining.","Sagittarius grows by learning that real freedom includes follow-through, and that some of the richest discoveries come from staying, not just from moving on.")
B.ay9=new A.iy(B.eU,"Capricorn is the zodiac's builder: a cardinal earth sign ruled by Saturn, oriented toward long-term achievement, discipline, and structures built to outlast any single season.","Disciplined, ambitious, and remarkably patient, Capricorn achieves through sustained effort rather than shortcuts. This sign's quiet reliability often makes it the person others lean on in a crisis.","Capricorn's drive can harden into workaholism, excessive self-criticism, or a difficulty relaxing that leaves little room for anything beyond the next goal.","Capricorn tends to keep emotion controlled and private, preferring to process feelings alone before showing any sign of vulnerability to others.","Capricorn communicates in a measured, practical, and often reserved way, saving its words for when they carry real weight rather than speaking simply to fill silence.","In love, Capricorn is deeply committed once it decides to invest, showing devotion through stability and long-term planning rather than dramatic gestures. Patience and consistency from a partner matter more to this sign than romance alone.","Capricorn friendships are few but genuinely enduring, often built over years of consistent, quiet reliability rather than constant contact. This sign shows up seriously when it truly matters.","At home, Capricorn often becomes the responsible one, managing practical family matters and long-term planning. Letting others share the load, rather than carrying it all alone, is a genuine lifelong practice.","Capricorn excels in business, law, engineering, or any field that rewards long-term strategy and disciplined execution. This sign is built for climbing toward a clear, worthwhile summit.","Financially, Capricorn is typically disciplined and long-term minded, planning carefully for security and status alike. This sign's challenge is allowing itself to enjoy the results of its own hard-earned success.","Capricorn's creativity shows through mastery built over time \u2014 architecture, craftsmanship, or any art form where patient, structured effort produces something built to last.","Capricorn's spirituality often centers on legacy, responsibility, and the long arc of a meaningful life, treating discipline itself as a spiritual practice.","Capricorn pairs comfortably with fellow earth signs Taurus and Virgo, sharing its practical values. Water signs Scorpio and Pisces add emotional depth, while a Cancer partner \u2014 its opposite sign \u2014 offers a meaningful balance between ambition and nurturing.","Capricorn's shadow includes coldness, ruthless ambition at others' expense, or measuring self-worth entirely by status and achievement.","Capricorn grows by learning that rest is not the opposite of ambition, and that its worth was never only about what it accomplishes.")
B.ayk=new A.iy(B.dR,"Aquarius is the zodiac's visionary: a fixed air sign ruled traditionally by Saturn and, in modern astrology, by Uranus, oriented toward the future, the collective, and genuine independence of thought.","Original, humanitarian, and intellectually independent, Aquarius brings fresh perspective and a real concern for the greater good. This sign is rarely afraid to think differently from everyone else.","Aquarius' independence can tip into detachment, an aloofness that keeps others at arm's length, or stubbornly holding an unconventional position simply because it is unconventional.","Aquarius tends to process emotion intellectually, sometimes analyzing a feeling rather than fully residing in it. Close friends often see far more warmth than casual acquaintances ever glimpse.","Aquarius communicates in an original, sometimes unconventional way, genuinely enjoying debate and unusual ideas. Emotional topics can be approached more comfortably through logic than through raw feeling.","In love, Aquarius needs real intellectual connection and enough independence to remain fully itself within the relationship. Clinginess or excessive conventionality tends to push this sign away quickly.","Aquarius often maintains a wide, eclectic network built around shared causes and ideas rather than close emotional intimacy alone. This sign is a famously loyal friend to a cause and to the people who share it.","At home, Aquarius may resist rigid family traditions in favor of forging its own path, while still caring deeply about the family's wellbeing in its own, sometimes unconventional way.","Aquarius thrives in technology, activism, science, or any field that rewards original thinking and forward-looking vision. Conformity for its own sake rarely sits well with this sign.","Financially, Aquarius can be unpredictable, sometimes investing in unconventional ideas or causes rather than conventional security. A flexible but structured plan suits this sign better than rigid rules.","Aquarius' creativity is inventive and often ahead of its time \u2014 technology, futurist design, or any art form that challenges convention outright.","Aquarius approaches spirituality through a humanitarian, often unconventional lens, more interested in collective progress and universal ideals than in traditional ritual.","Aquarius connects naturally with fellow air signs Gemini and Libra, sharing its intellectual curiosity. Fire signs Aries and Sagittarius match its independence, while a Leo partner \u2014 its opposite sign \u2014 offers a compelling balance of individuality and warmth.","Aquarius' shadow includes emotional coldness, contrarianism for its own sake, or a superiority that dismisses others' feelings as simply less rational.","Aquarius grows by learning that genuine connection does not require sacrificing its individuality, and that emotional vulnerability is its own form of progress.")
B.ayi=new A.iy(B.dS,"Pisces closes the zodiac wheel as its final sign: a mutable water sign ruled traditionally by Jupiter and, in modern astrology, by Neptune, dissolving boundaries between self and other, real and imagined.","Compassionate, imaginative, and deeply intuitive, Pisces feels its way toward genuine empathy that few other signs can match. This sign's creativity often draws directly from a rich inner world.","Pisces' porous boundaries can lead to escapism, difficulty saying no, or absorbing others' emotions so completely that its own needs get lost in the process.","Pisces feels everything, often all at once, and can struggle to separate its own emotions from the emotional atmosphere around it. A gentle, low-stimulation environment helps this sign recover its footing.","Pisces communicates through imagery, metaphor, and feeling more naturally than through blunt, literal statement, sometimes leaving listeners to interpret what it truly means.","In love, Pisces is romantic, deeply devoted, and often idealistic, giving generously of its emotional self. A partner who respects its need for both closeness and quiet retreat keeps this bond healthy.","Pisces is the friend who listens without judgment and offers genuine emotional refuge, though it needs friends who also check in on Pisces, since this sign rarely asks for help directly.","At home, Pisces often absorbs the family's emotional undercurrents, sometimes becoming the unofficial emotional caretaker. Learning to set gentle boundaries within the family is an important, ongoing practice.","Pisces excels in the arts, healing professions, counseling, or any field that rewards empathy and imagination. Rigid, purely transactional environments tend to feel draining over time.","Financially, Pisces can be generous to a fault and easily loses track of practical details amid bigger emotional or creative priorities. A simple, automated system helps keep finances steady without requiring constant attention.","Creativity is Pisces' native language \u2014 music, poetry, visual art, or film that channels emotion and imagination directly, often with striking, dreamlike originality.","Pisces is naturally drawn to the mystical and the transcendent, often feeling a spiritual connection to something larger than itself well before it can fully articulate what that connection is.","Pisces bonds deeply with fellow water signs Cancer and Scorpio, who share its emotional depth. Earth signs Taurus and Capricorn offer grounding, while a Virgo partner \u2014 its opposite sign \u2014 provides a valuable balance of structure and flow.","Pisces' shadow includes escapism, self-victimization, or a martyr-like tendency to dissolve its own needs entirely into someone else's.","Pisces grows by learning that boundaries are an act of self-compassion, not selfishness, and that it can stay compassionate without disappearing into someone else's story.")
