B.alJ=new A.jR(B.aj,"The Sun is the chart's core: not one planet among many but the organizing center everything else orbits, astrologically as well as physically. It describes fundamental identity, purpose, and the quality of life-force a person expresses when simply being most fully themselves.","Identity, vitality, purpose, ego, self-expression, and will.","Associated across cultures with kingship, divinity, and life-giving light \u2014 the visible source without which nothing else in the chart would be seen at all.","Rules Leo.","In fire signs the Sun burns visibly and expressively; in earth signs it expresses identity through tangible achievement and reliability; in air signs through ideas, connection, and social identity; in water signs through feeling, intuition, and emotional depth rather than outward display.","A highly public, identity-defining placement \u2014 Sun in an angular house often makes purpose and selfhood a visible, central life theme rather than a private undercurrent.","Identity expressed through building and stabilizing something \u2014 resources, creativity, shared intimacy, or community, depending on the specific succedent house.","Identity expressed more through process than through a fixed public role \u2014 learning, service, philosophy, or inner life, depending on the specific cadent house.","Trines and sextiles to the Sun tend to bring ease, confidence, and natural support for self-expression from whatever the other planet represents.","Squares and oppositions to the Sun often show friction between core identity and whatever the other planet demands \u2014 real growth usually comes from integrating rather than suppressing either side.",'A conjunction to the Sun blends that planet\'s themes directly into core identity \u2014 often intensifying it, sometimes to the point of the other planet feeling "used up" by how strongly the Sun expresses it.',null,"The Sun's yearly transit through the signs marks the seasonal zodiac calendar itself; its transits to natal points highlight that placement for a short, personally significant window once a year (including, at the Solar Return, the birthday itself).")
B.alF=new A.jR(B.ay,"The Moon governs the inner, instinctive, and emotional self: the reactions that happen before conscious thought catches up, and the conditions under which a person actually feels safe.","Emotion, instinct, habit, nurturing, memory, and comfort.","Tied across traditions to motherhood, the tides, and cyclical renewal \u2014 reflecting rather than generating light, much as mood reflects underlying need.","Rules Cancer.","In fire signs emotional reactions come fast and openly; in earth signs comfort comes through routine and material security; in air signs through conversation and mental processing; in water signs (its natural home) with the most direct, unfiltered emotional depth.","Emotional life becomes a visible, central part of identity or public role \u2014 moods and instincts are less hidden than average.","Emotional security tied closely to resources, creative expression, intimacy, or community, depending on the house.","Emotional life processed more privately \u2014 through learning, daily routine, belief, or solitude, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to the Moon bring emotional ease and instinctive support from whatever the other planet represents.","Squares and oppositions to the Moon often show tension between emotional needs and whatever the other planet demands, sometimes surfacing as moodiness until the underlying need is addressed directly.","A conjunction to the Moon blends that planet's themes into instinctive emotional response \u2014 the other planet's energy is felt, not just thought.",null,"The Moon moves fastest of all bodies, transiting the whole zodiac in about a month \u2014 its transits are short, mood-coloring windows rather than long developments, which is why the Daily Card treats the Moon's current sign and phase as a key daily ingredient.")
B.alG=new A.jR(B.bu,"Mercury governs the mind in its everyday, functional sense: thinking, talking, learning, and the countless small exchanges of information that make up ordinary communication.","Communication, thought, learning, reasoning, and travel.","Named for the swift messenger god, moving quickly between the planets as its namesake moved between realms \u2014 fitting for the fastest planet in daily sky-watching besides the Moon.","Rules Gemini and Virgo.","In fire signs thinking is quick and impulsive; in earth signs practical and detail-oriented; in air signs (its most natural home) abstract, curious, and socially fluent; in water signs intuitive, feeling-informed, sometimes less linear.","Communication and thinking become a visible, central part of identity or public role \u2014 often shows up as a naturally talkative or intellectually engaged public presence.","Thinking oriented toward practical outcomes \u2014 resources, creative projects, intimate understanding, or shared goals, depending on the house.","Mercury's natural cadent-house comfort zone \u2014 learning, routine information processing, philosophy, or introspection, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Mercury bring mental ease and clear communication in whatever area the other planet represents.","Squares and oppositions to Mercury often show friction between clear thinking and whatever the other planet demands \u2014 miscommunication or overthinking until it's consciously worked through.","A conjunction to Mercury pulls that planet's themes directly into how someone thinks and talks about them \u2014 often quite literally, as a frequent topic of conversation.","Mercury retrograde is astrology's most famous retrograde period, traditionally associated with communication mishaps, travel delays, and technology hiccups \u2014 and, more constructively, as a good window for review, revision, and reconnecting rather than launching something brand new.","Mercury's transits move quickly and mark short windows where communication, information, or short travel around a given life area becomes more active.")
B.alN=new A.jR(B.aQ,"Venus governs attraction, affection, and value: what a person finds beautiful, who and what they're drawn to, and the way they seek harmony in relationships and surroundings alike.","Love, beauty, harmony, values, and pleasure.","Named for the goddess of love and beauty, and traditionally called both the morning and evening star \u2014 fitting for a planet concerned with both romance's dawn and its steadier evening warmth.","Rules Taurus and Libra.","In fire signs love is bold and enthusiastic; in earth signs sensual, loyal, and grounded in tangible affection; in air signs social, intellectual, and idea-driven; in water signs deeply emotional and romantically intuitive.","Charm, aesthetics, and relational warmth become a visible, central part of identity or public role.","Venus's natural succedent-house comfort zone \u2014 values, love, and harmony expressed through resources, creativity, intimacy, or community, depending on the house.","Affection and aesthetic sense expressed more through process than display \u2014 in learning, daily habits, belief, or inner life, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Venus bring ease in love, aesthetics, and social warmth wherever the other planet touches.","Squares and oppositions to Venus often show tension between the desire for harmony and whatever the other planet demands \u2014 sometimes surfacing as people-pleasing until a more honest balance is found.","A conjunction to Venus adds charm, warmth, and aesthetic sensibility to that planet's themes \u2014 often making them easier to enjoy, though sometimes at the cost of being fully honest about them.","Venus retrograde periods are traditionally linked to reevaluating relationships and values \u2014 old flames resurfacing, or a genuine reassessment of what (and who) actually feels worth investing in.","Venus's transits mark windows of heightened social warmth, aesthetic sensitivity, or romantic opportunity around whatever life area it moves through.")
B.alI=new A.jR(B.aV,"Mars governs drive, desire, and assertiveness: the willingness to act, compete, and pursue what is wanted rather than simply hope for it.","Action, desire, courage, conflict, and physical energy.","Named for the god of war, and traditionally read as the more aggressive, combative counterpart to Venus's harmony \u2014 together the classical pairing of attraction and pursuit.","Traditional ruler of Scorpio; modern and traditional ruler of Aries.","In fire signs (its most natural home) action is direct and immediate; in earth signs disciplined and results-focused; in air signs strategic and debate-driven; in water signs intense but more internally held, surfacing through emotional determination rather than open confrontation.","Assertiveness and drive become a visible, central part of identity or public role \u2014 often a genuinely competitive or highly active public presence.","Drive channeled into building something concrete \u2014 resources, creative output, intimacy, or shared goals, depending on the house.","Energy expressed through sustained effort in process rather than a single decisive act \u2014 learning, daily work, belief, or inner struggle, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Mars bring confident, well-directed energy and healthy assertiveness wherever the other planet touches.","Squares and oppositions to Mars often generate real friction or impatience \u2014 genuinely useful when it drives constructive action, genuinely costly when it tips into unchecked conflict.","A conjunction to Mars energizes that planet's themes, often considerably \u2014 adding drive and urgency, for better and for worse.","Mars retrograde periods are traditionally read as a time when direct action doesn't land as expected \u2014 better suited to reassessing strategy and unfinished conflicts than launching a brand-new pursuit.","Mars's transits mark windows of heightened energy, motivation, or friction around whatever life area it moves through \u2014 genuinely good timing for decisive action, if channeled deliberately.")
B.alL=new A.jR(B.bR,"Jupiter governs growth, optimism, and expansion: the impulse to reach further, believe bigger, and trust that things can genuinely get better.","Growth, luck, optimism, wisdom, generosity, and abundance.",'Named for the king of the Roman gods, and traditionally called the "Greater Benefic" \u2014 the largest planet in the sky read, fittingly, as the astrological symbol of largeness itself: of opportunity, faith, and sheer scale.',"Traditional ruler of Pisces; modern and traditional ruler of Sagittarius.","In fire signs (its most natural home) growth is adventurous and confident; in earth signs practical and steadily accumulated; in air signs intellectual and socially expansive; in water signs spiritual, compassionate, and emotionally generous.","Optimism and a sense of expansive possibility become a visible, central part of identity or public role.","Growth channeled into building lasting abundance \u2014 resources, creative work, intimacy, or community, depending on the house.","Jupiter's natural cadent-house comfort zone \u2014 growth through learning, service, philosophy, or inner development, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Jupiter bring luck, generosity, and easy growth wherever the other planet touches \u2014 genuinely one of the more welcome aspect patterns to have.","Squares and oppositions to Jupiter can show overconfidence, excess, or overpromising in whatever the other planet represents \u2014 growth without enough grounding.","A conjunction to Jupiter amplifies that planet's themes considerably, usually for the better, though sometimes past a healthy scale if left unchecked.","Jupiter retrograde periods are traditionally read as a time for internal growth and reflection on belief and opportunity, rather than outward expansion.","Jupiter's roughly year-long transit through each sign marks a broad theme of growth and opportunity for everyone, felt most personally wherever it activates an individual's own placements.")
B.alK=new A.jR(B.b4,"Saturn governs structure, discipline, and time: the boundaries, responsibilities, and long slow effort that eventually produce something durable enough to last.","Discipline, responsibility, limits, mastery, and maturity.",'Named for the god of time and harvest, and traditionally called the "Greater Malefic" not out of malice but because growth here always requires real, sometimes uncomfortable, effort \u2014 the harvest that only comes after patient tending.',"Traditional ruler of Aquarius; modern and traditional ruler of Capricorn.","In fire signs discipline is applied to bold ambition; in earth signs (its most natural home) to practical, tangible achievement; in air signs to structured thinking and long-term planning; in water signs to emotional maturity and the patient tending of lasting bonds.","Responsibility and long-term achievement become a visible, central part of identity or public role \u2014 often a reputation built slowly but built to last.","Discipline applied to building lasting security \u2014 resources, creative mastery, committed intimacy, or long-term community standing, depending on the house.","Structure applied through sustained process \u2014 rigorous learning, consistent daily discipline, firmly held belief, or serious inner work, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Saturn bring steady, earned support and staying power wherever the other planet touches.","Squares and oppositions to Saturn often show real restriction or self-doubt in whatever the other planet represents \u2014 hard, but frequently where the most durable long-term growth eventually comes from.","A conjunction to Saturn adds weight, seriousness, and structure to that planet's themes \u2014 sometimes felt as a limitation at first, often becoming a genuine strength once mastered.","Saturn retrograde periods are traditionally read as a time for reviewing and internally restructuring commitments and responsibilities, rather than taking on entirely new ones.","Saturn's roughly 2.5-year transit through each sign marks a long chapter of tests and consolidation, felt most personally around the Saturn Return (roughly ages 29, 58, and 87) when it returns to its own natal position.")
B.alM=new A.jR(B.cJ,"Uranus governs sudden change, independence, and innovation: the impulse to break from convention and the flashes of insight that arrive without warning.","Rebellion, innovation, freedom, sudden change, and originality.",'Named for the primordial sky god and discovered only in 1781, Uranus is read as the first of the modern, slower-moving "generational" planets \u2014 its placement by sign shapes a whole generation more than any one individual.',"Modern ruler of Aquarius (traditionally ruled by Saturn).","In fire signs rebellion is bold and immediate; in earth signs innovation is applied practically, often to systems and institutions; in air signs (its natural home) intellectually radical and socially progressive; in water signs emotionally unpredictable, breaking old patterns of feeling rather than thought.","Independence and unconventionality become a visible, central part of identity or public role.","Sudden change touching resources, creative expression, intimacy, or community \u2014 depending on the house, in ways that resist being settled or predictable.","Innovation expressed through ongoing intellectual or spiritual restlessness \u2014 learning, routine-breaking, belief, or inner insight, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Uranus bring welcome, generally constructive surprises and a comfortable relationship with change wherever the other planet touches.","Squares and oppositions to Uranus often bring disruptive, harder-to-predict upheaval in whatever the other planet represents.","A conjunction to Uranus makes that planet's themes unpredictable and prone to sudden change \u2014 exciting, but rarely stable.","Uranus spends roughly five months of every year retrograde \u2014 traditionally read as a time when change is processed and integrated internally rather than acted out visibly.",'Uranus\'s roughly 7-year transit through each sign marks a generational theme of disruption and innovation, felt personally most around the "Uranus opposition" in midlife (roughly age 40-42) when it opposes its own natal position.')
B.alH=new A.jR(B.cr,"Neptune governs dreams, spirituality, and dissolution of boundaries: imagination, compassion, and the pull toward something larger and less clearly defined than the ordinary material world.","Imagination, spirituality, compassion, illusion, and idealism.","Named for the god of the sea, and read as a planet of fluid, boundary-dissolving depth \u2014 as hard to hold onto directly as water itself, for better (transcendence, art, compassion) and for worse (confusion, escapism, deception).","Modern ruler of Pisces (traditionally ruled by Jupiter).","In fire signs idealism is passionate and visionary; in earth signs imagination is applied practically, often through art or healing work; in air signs expressed intellectually, as idealistic or utopian thinking; in water signs (its natural home) as deep, unfiltered emotional and spiritual sensitivity.","Idealism, imagination, or spiritual sensitivity become a visible, central part of identity or public role.","Dreams and ideals touching resources, creative work, intimacy, or community \u2014 often in ways that resist clean, concrete definition.","Neptune's natural cadent-house comfort zone \u2014 spirituality and imagination expressed through learning, service, belief, or inner life, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Neptune bring inspiration, compassion, and creative flow wherever the other planet touches.","Squares and oppositions to Neptune often bring confusion, idealization, or difficulty seeing whatever the other planet represents clearly \u2014 worth double-checking assumptions rather than trusting the first impression.","A conjunction to Neptune blurs and softens that planet's themes \u2014 beautiful and inspiring at its best, foggy or self-deceiving at its most unchecked.","Neptune spends roughly five months of every year retrograde \u2014 traditionally read as a time when illusions are more likely to be seen through, for better or worse.","Neptune's roughly 14-year transit through each sign marks a generational theme of collective idealism or disillusionment, felt personally in wherever it touches an individual's own placements.")
B.alE=new A.jR(B.ch,"Pluto governs transformation at the deepest level: death and rebirth in the broad sense of anything that must fully end before something truly new can begin, along with the hidden, sometimes uncomfortable truths that power and intimacy both eventually surface.","Transformation, power, intensity, the unconscious, and rebirth.","Named for the god of the underworld, and read \u2014 despite its reclassification as a dwarf planet astronomically \u2014 as a full participant in astrological tradition since its 1930 discovery: the slowest-moving, most generationally-scaled of the outer planets.","Modern ruler of Scorpio (traditionally ruled by Mars).","In fire signs transformation is fought for directly and visibly; in earth signs it reshapes material structures and institutions; in air signs it transforms ideas, communication, and collective thought; in water signs (its natural home) it operates at the deepest emotional and psychological level.","Intensity and personal power become a visible, central part of identity or public role \u2014 often someone who is hard to overlook and slow to fully reveal.","Transformation touching resources, creative work, intimacy, or community \u2014 frequently the house placement most associated with genuinely reshaping a whole area of life rather than merely adjusting it.","Pluto's influence unfolding gradually through process \u2014 learning, service, belief, or the unconscious itself, depending on the house.","Trines and sextiles to Pluto bring the ability to handle intensity and transformation constructively wherever the other planet touches.","Squares and oppositions to Pluto often bring power struggles or compulsive intensity around whatever the other planet represents \u2014 frequently pointing to exactly what most needs to be consciously faced rather than avoided.","A conjunction to Pluto intensifies that planet's themes considerably, often bringing them into contact with real personal power and eventual transformation.","Pluto spends roughly five to six months of every year retrograde \u2014 traditionally read as a time when transformation happens internally, beneath the surface, before it becomes visible.","Pluto's extremely slow transit (well over a decade in each sign) marks generational transformation more than a personal timing tool, felt most personally through its harder aspects to an individual's own placements.")
B.o9=new A.by([B.aj,B.alJ,B.ay,B.alF,B.bu,B.alG,B.aQ,B.alN,B.aV,B.alI,B.bR,B.alL,B.b4,B.alK,B.cJ,B.alM,B.cr,B.alH,B.ch,B.alE],A.a6("by<dp,jR>"))
B.aiU=new A.by([B.aj,"Sun",B.ay,"Moon",B.bu,"Mercury",B.aQ,"Venus",B.aV,"Mars",B.bR,"Jupiter",B.b4,"Saturn",B.cJ,"Uranus",B.cr,"Neptune",B.ch,"Pluto"],t.N2)
B.zU=new A.by([B.aj,"core identity and vitality",B.ay,"emotional instincts and comfort needs",B.bu,"communication style and thinking",B.aQ,"affection, values, and what feels lovable",B.aV,"drive, desire, and assertiveness",B.bR,"optimism and appetite for growth",B.b4,"sense of commitment and structure",B.cJ,"need for independence and surprise",B.cr,"dreams, ideals, and imagination",B.ch,"capacity for transformation and intensity"],t.N2)
B.aaB=s(["The Sun's Clear Light","Sunlit Purpose","The Sun's Quiet Confidence","A Sunlit Turning Point"],t.s)
B.a2D=s(["The Quiet Moon","Lunar Release","Tides of Feeling","The Moon's Undertow"],t.s)
